ref_dict.def:classSc:
\begin{definition}[Symmetric function pair]\label{def:classSc}
We say 
$(f,g)$ is a symmetric  function pair if  there exists a decomposition pair $\{(A_k, B_k),\ k = 1,\dots, K\}$, a sequence of different numbers $\{s_k\}_{k= 1}^K$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
 f=\sum_{1\leq k\leq K}s_k\chi_{A_k}, \quad g=\sum_{1\leq k\leq K}s_k\chi_{B_k},
\end{equation*}
and 
\begin{equation*}
    \int_{\T} (f+ g)(x) \d x= 0.
\end{equation*}
The set of all symmetric function pairs is denoted by $\mathcal{S}^2_c$.
\end{definition}

