Let $A$ be a finite-dimensional algebra. Then $A$ is derived-discrete if and only if $A$ is derived equivalent to either a hereditary algebra of Dynkin type or $\Lambda(r,n,m)$ for some integers $m\ge 0$ and $n\ge r\ge 1$.
