\label{Th-SynthesExistenceSW}
    Let $d\in\{1,2\}$, $\lambda,\omega\in\mathbb R$ and $\gamma>0$. Denote by $\mu_0$ the lowest eigenvalue of $-A$. In each of the following situation, there exists a positive solution of
\begin{equation}
    -A\phi-\lambda|\phi|^{2\gamma}\phi+\omega \phi = 0. \label{Eq-StationaryAGP}
\end{equation}
 in $\mathrm{D}\left(\sqrt{|A|}\right)$,
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $\lambda>0$ and $\omega>-\mu_0$,
        \item $\lambda = 0$ and $\omega=\mu_0$,
        \item $\lambda<0$ and $\omega<-\mu_0$.
    \end{itemize}
    In every other cases, there is no non-trivial non-negative solution in $\mathrm{D}\left(\sqrt{|A|}\right)$.,

