[Main Theorem]
\label{mainThm}
For some $a_0 \ge 1$ and $N \in (0, 2)$, let $V : \R^2 \to \R$ satisfy 
\begin{equation}
\label{Vbound}
\left\vertV(w)\right\vert \le a_0^2 \left< w \right>^{-N}.
\end{equation}
Assume that $u : \R^2 \to \R$ is a solution to 
\begin{equation}
\label{ellipEq}
- \Delta u + V u = 0 \, \text{ in } \R^2
\end{equation}
with the properties that 
\begin{equation}
\label{solNorm}
\left\vertu(0)\right\vert = 1
\end{equation}
and for each $w \in \R^2$,
\begin{equation}
\label{uBound}
\left\vertu(w)\right\vert \le \exp\pr{c_0 \left\vertw\right\vert^{1 - \frac N 2}}.
\end{equation}
For every $\varepsilon \in \left( 0, \frac N 2 \right) $, there exists ${R}_0(N, a_0, c_0, \varepsilon) > 0$ so that whenever $R \ge {R}_0$, it holds that
\begin{equation}
\label{uLower}
\inf_{\left\vertw_0\right\vert = R} \left\| u\right\|_{L^\infty\left( B_1(w_0) \right) } \ge \exp\pr{-R^{1 - \frac N 2 + \varepsilon}}.
\end{equation}

