\label{T_main}
    Let $A\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ ($d\geq 3$) be a set with positive reach with $\dim A\leq 2$ and let $a\in A$ be such that $\dim(\operatorname{Tan}(A,a))=1$. Then there exist a $\operatorname{B}$-set $B\subset\mathbb{R}^2\subset\mathbb{R}^d$, a multirotation $\rho:\mathbb{R}^d\to\mathbb{R}^d$ associated with $T_1(B)$ and a $C^{1,1}$-diffeomorphism $\Phi:U\subset\mathbb{R}^d\to\mathbb{R}^d$ such that $0\in U$, $a=\Phi(0)$, $\rho(B)\subset U$ and $\Phi(\rho(B))$ is a neighbourhood of $a$ in $A$.

