Let us consider now the case $a\in T_1^-(A)$. Choose $0<r<\reach A$ and let $u$ be the unit vector such that $\Tan(A,a)=\{tu:\, t\geq 0\}$. Denoting $S:=\{a+tu:\, -\frac r4\leq t< 0\}$ and $A^*:=A\cup S$, we have clearly $a\in T_1^+(A^*)$ and \cite[Lemma 3.8]{RZ17} gives $\reach A^* \geq r/4$. We apply the already proved assertion and find a $\B_+$-set $B^*$ and a multirotation $\rho^*$ associated with $T_1(B^*)$ such that $(A^*,a)\approx(\rho^*(B^*),0)$. 
By Remark~\ref{oekv1}~(i) there exist a $C^{1,1}$-diffeomorphism $\Phi$ defined on a neighbourhood $U$ of $a$ and $\ep>0$ such that 
\begin{equation} \label{AB}
