\label{thm:diagonal_to_ratio}
If the following conjecture holds:
\begin{conjecture}\label{conj:weak.mult.RDC}
    For every $s, t, k \in \N$ such that $st \le k^2$ we have that    
    \begin{equation*}    
        R(s,t) \le R(k, k).
    \end{equation*}
\end{conjecture}
and $\lim\limits_{k \to \infty} \frac{\log(R(k,k))}{k}$ exists and is equal to $\mathcal{L}$, then
\begin{equation*}     
    f(n)=\big(\mathcal{L}^2+o(1)\big)\frac{n}{(\log n)^2} .
\end{equation*}

