 and Anderson's shifted-ball inequality \cite{Anderson}.
 Fix $\delta > 0$ such that
 \begin{equation}\label{ltdb}
 \frac{\lambda(\theta)+\delta}{\rho}<\beta.
 \end{equation}
 It follows from the above and Proposition \ref{pr:BC:H} that
 \begin{align*}
 I_2 &\le 
 \iint_{\substack{x,y\in K:\\\varepsilon_1^\rho < |x-y|\le 2\varepsilon_2^\rho}}
 \frac{\mu(\d x)\,\mu(\d y)}{\P\left\{\sup_{t\in[|x-y|^{1/\rho}, \varepsilon_2]} 
 |H(t\,,y)| \le \theta\right\}}\\
 &\lesssim\iint_{\substack{x,y\in K:\\\varepsilon_1^\rho < |x-y|\le 2\varepsilon_2^\rho}}\left( \frac{\varepsilon_2}{|x-y|^{1/\rho}}\right)^{\lambda(\theta)+\delta}\,
 \mu(\d x)\,\mu(\d y)
 =\mathscr{o}(1) \iint_{K \times K}
 \frac{\mu(\d x)\,\mu(\d y)}{|x-y|^{(\lambda(\theta)+\delta)/\rho}},
 \end{align*}
