\begin{equation}
\label{eq:one-armcrit}
 c\, (\log N)^{-1/2} \leq \theta(a,N)\big\vert_{a=0} \leq C\, (\log N)^{-1/2},
\end{equation}
Our main result determines the scaling of the quantity $\theta(a, N)$, giving precise meaning to \eqref{eq:scaling-new}.

