$\capacity_{\mathbb R^2}^{\tau}(A)\equiv \capacity_{\mathbb R^2}(A)$ denote the corresponding capacity, defined in one of several possible ways in terms of the variational principle
\begin{equation} \label{eq:cap_time_change_bm}
 \big(\capacity_{\mathbb R^2}(A)\big)^{-1} = \inf_{\mu}\int_0^1 \int_0^1 \frac{ 2\color{Black}}{\pi} K_0\big( 2 \color{Black} |x-y|\big) \,d\mu(x)\,d\mu(y), 
\end{equation}
where the infimum ranges over all probability measures $\mu$ on $A$ and
\begin{equation} \label{eq:K_0}
 K_0(s)\stackrel{\text{def.}}{=} \int_{0}^\infty \frac{1}{2 t}
 \exp\left\{-\frac{s^2}{4t}-t\right\} \,dt, \quad s > 0,
 \end{equation}
