mcq.question:
Let $G\subseteq \mathrm{GL}(\mathrm V)$ be the connected component of a classical group over a finite field, attached to a vector space $\mathrm V$, and let $\chi$ be a multiplicative character of the scalar field of $\mathrm V$ (equivalently, of the center $Z(\mathrm{GL}(\mathrm V))$). Define a function on $G$ by
$$
\mathrm K_{\mathrm V}^{\chi}(g)=
\begin{cases}
\chi\bigl(\det(\operatorname{id}_{\mathrm V}+g)\bigr), & \det(\operatorname{id}_{\mathrm V}+g)\neq 0,\\
0, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
$$
(Here $\operatorname{id}_{\mathrm V}$ is the identity on $\mathrm V$.) If a function on $G$ is called stable when it is constant on stable conjugacy classes, which statement holds for every such pair $(G,\chi)$?

